Grieving women lay postcards to prevent suicides on decks.
Two women who have lost loved ones out of suicide are trying to prevent others from taking their own lives.
Sharon Davis and Kelly Humphreys posted, on a Welsh bridge, postcards containing inspiring messages and phone numbers that people can call for help.
Ms. Davis’ son, Tyler, was 13 years old when he started suffering from depression and committed suicide at the age of 18.
“I don’t want any parent to feel what I’m forced to feel every day,” she said.
Davis, a 45-year-old living in Lydney, said her son was a promising leader with a contagious smile.
“Everybody knew him for his smile.
They always said that his smile illuminated any room.”
However, he let go of his job before he died, since he found himself “in a very dark place.”
In 2014, it was Tyler’s 11-year-old brother who reunited with his brother after he committed suicide.
