Ms. Davis created the cards “to let people know that there are people you can go to and talk to, even if it’s a friend.
Don’t remain silent – you have to talk.”
Ms. Humphreys, a long-time friend of Ms. Davis, has lost Mark, her partner for 15 years, shortly after her mother's death.
“He didn’t say he’d feel dead, depressed or otherwise,” she said.
“A few days before Christmas, we’ve seen a change in attitude.
He was at his lowest on Christmas Day – when the children opened their gifts, he didn’t have eye contact with them or anything.”
She said her death was a huge trauma to them, but they have to get by: “It’s heartbreaking for the family.
It's destroying us.
