Pelosi, leader of the parliamentary minority, called Supreme Court candidate Brett Kavanaugh “hysterical” and said he was unfit to serve on the Supreme Court because of his disposition.
Pelosi made the comments as part of an interview at the Texas Tribune Festival in Austin, Texas on Saturday.
I couldn’t help but think that if a woman had behaved in this way, they would have called her “hysterical,” Pelosi said of her reaction to Kavanaugh’s testimony before the Senate Judicial Committee last Thursday.
Kavanaugh emotionally denied the allegations that he sexually assaulted Dr. Christine Blasey Ford when they were both teenagers.
